{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy","id":1498727,"title":"The Glasaugen - Mastigos Forces / Space Homebrew legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-03T20:17:46-08:00","id":1498727,"title":"The Glasaugen - Mastigos Forces / Space Homebrew legacy","content":"<u><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Glasaugen</span></span></span></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Spies, Big Brothers (Derogatory)</i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> The Cold War has a reputation for espionage and surveillance and this is due to the high prevalence of espionage and surveillance. The Wise were not immune to the effects of paranoia brought about during this time. One such effect was the Glasaugen (\u201cGlass Eyes\u201d in English), a legacy with the intent to master the surveillance states that were emerging. Both the Guardians of the Veil and the Panopticon Ministry practice this legacy and both claim the other stole it from them. All that is known for sure is that the legacy originated in Germany, if the founding mage was a Soviet or a member of the Allies is unknown but there was no shortage of mages on both sides who joined. Until the fall of the Soviet Union the Glasaugen fought its own cold war within its ranks, as both the Seers and Guardians tried to eradicate the members on the other side, and also the Allied and Soviet mages did the same. While the national conflict ended in 1992, the war between the awakened continues. Assassinations are not as common nowadays, but both sides are keeping an eye on the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Glasaugen see the enlargement, use, and maintenance of a surveillance state as a holy endeavor and in this endeavor they have won. Everyone should be watched or, if it is not possible to actually watch them, they should be made to believe they are being watched. Those who believe their every move is being observed are less likely to act outside of societal norms and therefore, less likely to awaken. Those spies within the Guardians are more likely to emphasize that those who are watched are more easily to maneuver into the labyrinths if they are found unworthy, but this philosophy has led to tensions with the Free Council, who see them as a branch of the Panopticon Ministry that have infiltrated the Pentacle. Of course the Guardians deny this, but stories of members of this legacy defecting to the servants of the Eye are much more common than the reverse.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is not just the surveillance state that is a matter of interest to the Glass Eyes, they also study the mysteries of parasocial sympathy. So much of their work involves observing and learning about others who have no clue they exist. This still results in sympathetic connections, but they only go one way. These sympathies are considered sacred by the legacy, and if someone they are surveying ever needs to be killed the Glasaugen with the connection to them will never be the one required to perform the assassination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Many of the Glass Eyes come from intelligence agencies, with many more once being private investigators. Some are paranoid of &quot;big brother&quot; watching them and later discover that they have become what they feared.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Glasaugen dress inconspicuously, appropriate for whatever environment they find themselves in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Organization: </b>Like any intelligence agency, the Glass Eyes are organized from the top down, with those above giving orders to those below. Promotions within the legacy also come with the teaching of new attainments.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> Magic is holy when only the one performing the magic can see it. When the person who is being affected by magic has no clue the magic is happening, that is divinity. It is not divine in the sense that it is next to god, inspired by god, or a reflection of divinity. It is divinity within the fallen world. Magic, to The Glasaugen, is an expression of divine knowledge. Not abstract or philosophical knowledge, but useful, practical knowledge about a someone or something. You study a person, place, or thing (from the shadows) in order to build up a parasocial sympathetic connection to them so that you can perform magic, but the construction of that sort of sympathy is also magic. \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Doctrine and Magic</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mastigos </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Order: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Guardians of the Veil or the Panopticon Ministry</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Forces 2, Space 1, 2 dots in Subterfuge, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Computers, Investigation, Larceny, Stealth</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiation:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gather novel information on a target assigned by your mentor. The information needs to be novel to the initiate, not the mentor, and must be gathered without using magic.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcana: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forces</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Casting magic remotely through surveillance equipment (+1); Casting magic on someone you have investigated thoroughly (+2); If the mage successfully lied or hid information during the scene, or saw through a lie or found hidden information during the scene (+1-3 depending on significance of the lie or information); If the mage knows a secret about the target that the target is unaware that the mage knows (+1-3 depending on significance).</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shadow a target to learn information on them; Spend time watching security footage, live or recorded; Convince someone to act in line with society because they are being watched by some shadowy force.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Attainments</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Attainment: Information Everywhere</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The modern era is filled with radio waves, cell phones providing data, and people with iWatches on their wrists. While sleepers cannot interact with all this free floating data, the Glasaugen learn to be aware of it constantly. After an hour of meditation the mage is able to see data in the air. This attainment functions as \u201cTune In\u201d (Forces 1, MtAw 141) with reach for advanced duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optonal: Space 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Data is all around the mage, and so are the potential enemies shadowing her. The mage must learn to always see everything happening around them. This attainment activates with the same hour of mediation and functions as \u201cThe Outward and Inward Eye\u201d (Space 1, MtAw 174) with reach for advanced duration. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Second Attainment: Unseen by the Eyes of Others</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces 2, 3 dots in Subterfuge</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A spy must learn how to move through the world without being seen. This attainment allows the mage to do just this, after an hour of meditation the attainment acts as \u201cInvisibility\u201d (Forces 2, MtAw 143) with reach for advanced duration. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Space 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spies need to be able to get into places they aren\u2019t welcome and they learn early on how to. This attainment functions as \u201cBreak Boundary\u201d (Space 2, MtAw 174) with reach assigned to instant casting.</span> </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Third Attainment: Data Mining</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this point in a spies' understanding they are now able to transmit the data they are seeing, preventing others from seeing what they don\u2019t want them to see, or making sure that anything they want to be seen is seen. This attainment functions as \u201cTransmission\u201d (Forces 2, MtAw 144) with reach for instant casting and advanced duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Space 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Spies need to know as much about a target they are watching as possible, including where to find them and how to blackmail them if needed. This attainment helps with that by emulating \u201cCorrespondence\u201d (Space 1, MtAw 172) with reach for instant casting, sensory range, and to allow the mage to follow the trail of sympathetic links. While this does not give the spy the information they need per say, it does give them information on where to find it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fourth Attainment: Sight from Afar</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces 4, 4 dots in Subterfuge</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spy needs to be able to observe from afar, away from other mages who might be able to see through their disguises or magics. It is at this point in the training of the mage that they learn how to do so. This attainment functions as \u201cZoom In\u201d (Forces 2, MtAw 144) with reach for advanced duration and instant casting, along with the ability to zoom into the molecular level. This point in their training usually involves the study of science so that the mage can recognize poisons and other dangerous molecules. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Space 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Due to the conflict, both national and awakened, within the history of the legacy, and the legacies affinity to uncover sympathetic links, the spies developed a technique to hide their sympathetic links. This attainment functions as \u201cVeil Sympathy\u201d (Space 2, MtAw 175) with reach for advanced durations and and changing the primary factor to potency, and the bonus effect to hide </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>all</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> of their sympathetic links.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fifth Attainment: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From Dust to Ash</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Forces 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The final attainment allows the spies to kill those they are required to with a touch, vaporizing them. The attainment is withstood by Stamina, and is not a dramatic end. The person is simply vaporized on a cellular level, leaving nothing behind but a pile of ash to be blown away in the wind. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Space 5</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Throughout their career spies create and discover many sympathetic links, this attainment allows them to capitalize on these links. With an hour of work the attainment functions as \u201cCo-Location\u201d (Space 3, MtAw 176) with reach for advanced duration, with reach to create a stable portal between the two locations for the duration of the attainment, and with the ability to specify a Key needed to use the overlapped space (usually the key is themselves or something personal to them so rival spies cannot use their portal network).</span>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 03-08-2023, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T20:28:22-08:00","id":1498729,"title":"","content":"Hello there mages I came up with the idea of this legacy a while ago while reading the GotV book and they discussed a section where the Guardians were part of the intelligence agencies of the world. I couldn't come up with the 4th and 5th attainments in a way that made me happy so I decided not to worry about them. Probably would do something with the Electromagnetic Pulse spell, but who knows, maybe I'll finish this in the future.<br /> <br /> Thanks everyone here for the advice and help! And thanks to Magecord for all the input as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 12-07-2022, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T20:38:17-08:00","id":1498730,"title":"","content":"Interesting! I'm guessing the fact that they're a Mastigos Legacy helps get around the complications of the opposing membership being sympathetic Yantras for each other. What's the Theory behind their Legacy, and was its required knowledge base different before the widespread availability of computers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T20:53:22-08:00","id":1498732,"title":"","content":"The higher attainments depend on what you imagine exemplifes the legacy. Do they become masters of obtaining information, or do they shield themselves? Maybe they instead weaponize the info beyond just the mundane, opening doors more ably on people they have dirt on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T21:08:16-08:00","id":1498734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498730#post1498730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! I'm guessing the fact that they're a Mastigos Legacy helps get around the complications of the opposing membership being sympathetic Yantras for each other. What's the Theory behind their Legacy, and was its required knowledge base different before the widespread availability of computers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Surveillance technology was being developed during the Cold War, these mages sought to unlock the secrets that would come along with that, so no their required knowledge base was fairly similar, now its just even more relevant being computers are so wide spread, data is in the air at all times, and you many people's lives are free online. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the first attainment was different in the past, Influence Electricity perhaps? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T05:06:25-08:00","id":1498751,"title":"","content":"Minor question about the Space Apprentice Attainment; it's not at Sight Range, so do you imagine they're usually touching the target, or Aiming at them? Both make for interesting visuals.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind suggestions on the existing ones, I'd actually move <u>Scrying</u> up to Adept so it can use Sympathetic Range natively rather than needing to spend Mana. You could replace it in the Disciple slot with <u>Veil Sympathy</u> (Reach to Advanced Duration, Potency to Primary), which would make sense as a protective measure. Like Satchel said, it makes sense that a Mastigos Legacy could sustainably have both Seer and Pentacle houses.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, your Space Attainments seem to be more about observation, while the Forces ones are more generalized. <u>Locate Object</u> might be useful as a Disciple or higher. Instantly cause a touched subject to be trackable for an advanced duration, even if it leaves your presence. <br /> <br /> As TempleBuilder said, theme will matter for the Adept and Master Attainments. Again, the trend I'm reading in the Space side is enhancing the users observational power, so much as I'd like to recommend Advanced Duration <u>Force No Chains</u> in the Master slot, it does deviate from the pattern. <br /> <br /> <u>Web Weaver</u> (Especially if you allow the Time 2 expansion) would be a very useful at Advanced Duration, Instant Casting, and Potency Switch. You could get away with dropping Instant Casting (or Advanced Duration, if you don't mind reactivating it every few seconds), but it ultimately becomes a way to temporarily create <i>really</i> strong links to utilize while still being able to drop them at a moments notice.<br /> <br /> For the Forces side, a hologram duplicate would be a neat distraction power. Thats... Weaving, probably? Put it in at least Adept for Instant Casting and Advanced Duration. I'd actually say that you could modify <u>Invisibility</u> in the Apprentice Attainment to behave as a Forces version of <u>Machine Invisibility</u> that protects you from all visual-surveilance tech but not living sentinels, then put actual Forces <u>Invisibility</u> into the Adept slot. Put a hologram-generation power into the Master slot, then you'd be able to generate a duplicate to cover your sudden disappearance.<br /> <br /> Or possibly, swap <u>Transmission</u> and <u>Invisibility</u>. <u>Transmission</u> is still viable with one less Reach, while <u>Invisibility</u> works better (in my opinion) if it's Instant-Cast. Drop a hologram-dulpicate into the Adept slot then.<br /> <br /> <u>Rapid Access Memory</u> would make for an interesting capstone, although the Prime requirement doesn't really fit with the rest of the Legacy.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the ramble, design is fun. The Legacy looks good so far!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-04-2022, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T08:27:18-08:00","id":1498764,"title":"","content":"Fourth Attainment could be Zoom In, with Reach assigned to advanced duration, allowing them to see for miles and perceive dust sized particles. Now they no longer need to worry about being poisoned and can read lips at a distance whenever setting up a Scrying Window is inconvenient.<br /> <br /> The optional could be Secret Door, with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced duration and placing a Key. Now they can have their secret base protected from mundane detection, the area hiding their tools or incriminating evidence will not be found, nor will the locker they placed the dead drop in, unless its its someone in the know.<br /> <br /> The capstone could be Control Weather with instant use, advanced duration and drastic changes. With conjunctional Space 4, they can spend a mana to active Everywhere. Now the mage can have a meeting with a contact while heavy winds make it difficult to listen on their conversation. They can isolate enemies with a Blizzard, cause chaos in their base by sneaking in invisibly and creating an Inferno or destroy their important documents by having the building Flooded. All can be seen as freak accidents that do not betray their presence.<br /> <br /> The optional capstone could be Co-Location, creating a portal. Combined with Secret Room, this means they can have a vast secret network of infiltration. Reach is assigned to advanced duration, sensory range and creating a portal, with a mana spent on sympathetic range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-04-2022, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T12:44:59-08:00","id":1498784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498730#post1498730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting! I'm guessing the fact that they're a Mastigos Legacy helps get around the complications of the opposing membership being sympathetic Yantras for each other. What's the Theory behind their Legacy, and was its required knowledge base different before the widespread availability of computers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually after thinking about this over night I think Subterfuge makes more sense, computers isn't something that was widespread like you said, so it makes sense that it would have been a secondary thing that they studied. Thank you for the question! It's made the legacy better!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 12-06-2022, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T12:48:13-08:00","id":1498786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498751#post1498751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor question about the Space Apprentice Attainment; it's not at Sight Range, so do you imagine they're usually touching the target, or Aiming at them? Both make for interesting visuals.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind suggestions on the existing ones, I'd actually move <u>Scrying</u> up to Adept so it can use Sympathetic Range natively rather than needing to spend Mana. You could replace it in the Disciple slot with <u>Veil Sympathy</u> (Reach to Advanced Duration, Potency to Primary), which would make sense as a protective measure. Like Satchel said, it makes sense that a Mastigos Legacy could sustainably have both Seer and Pentacle houses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch! They are not suppose to be walking around touching people to gain information on their sympathetic connections, gonna have to move some things around. I was also thinking about including veil sympathy for the same reasons you and Satchel noted, it makes sense as a counter measure, both as a spy and a legacy that involves the Seers and the Diamond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T12:49:01-08:00","id":1498787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498764#post1498764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The optional could be Secret Door, with Reach assigned to instant use, advanced duration and placing a Key. Now they can have their secret base protected from mundane detection, the area hiding their tools or incriminating evidence will not be found, nor will the locker they placed the dead drop in, unless its its someone in the know.<br /> <br /> The optional capstone could be Co-Location, creating a portal. Combined with Secret Room, this means they can have a vast secret network of infiltration. Reach is assigned to advanced duration, sensory range and creating a portal, with a mana spent on sympathetic range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Love both of these suggestions, alright time to hit the drawing board again, thanks all for the feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T12:58:09-08:00","id":1498788,"title":"","content":"So it was an easy fix, moved the second attainment to 3 so it could have sensory range and added break boundaries as the second attainment, letting the spy go wherever they need to, dropped their abilities to scry as an attainment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 12-04-2022, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T22:07:17-08:00","id":1498813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy#post1498727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Space 4</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Due to the conflict, both national and awakened, within the history of the legacy, and the legacies affinity to uncover sympathetic links, the spies developed a technique to hide their sympathetic links. This attainment functions as \u201cVeil Sympathy\u201d (Space 2, MtAw 175) with reach for advanced durations and instant use, and the bonus effect to hide </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>all</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> of their sympathetic links. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Something to keep in mind; technically, since <u>Veil Sympathy</u> is Withstood by the strength of the veiled Connection, this will only obscure their Medium and Weak Connections. Switching Potency to Primary would get everything below Connected once you're a Master of Space, but the only way to hide Connected ties would be to attain Archmastery's hypothetical 6th dot.<br /> <br /> That being said, it's mostly me nit-picking based on RAW. I would recommend adding in some limiting factor though, to balance out a virtual no-sell on Sympathy-detection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T22:36:19-08:00","id":1498814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498813#post1498813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to keep in mind; technically, since <u>Veil Sympathy</u> is Withstood by the strength of the veiled Connection, this will only obscure their Medium and Weak Connections. Switching Potency to Primary would get everything below Connected once you're a Master of Space, but the only way to hide Connected ties would be to attain Archmastery's hypothetical 6th dot.<br /> <br /> That being said, it's mostly me nit-picking based on RAW. I would recommend adding in some limiting factor though, to balance out a virtual no-sell on Sympathy-detection.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The hiding of all sympathy links isn't covered by that huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T22:54:05-08:00","id":1498816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498814#post1498814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The hiding of all sympathy links isn't covered by that huh?</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>affects</i> all your links, but is also Withstood by them. I don't think you can choose to voluntarily forgo the Withstand to a spell that targets Connection; they're related but separate from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T22:58:30-08:00","id":1498817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498816#post1498816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It <i>affects</i> all your links, but is also Withstood by them. I don't think you can choose to voluntarily forgo the Withstand to a spell that targets Connection; they're related but separate from you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Makes sense, I'll bump that up to the 5th attainment then I think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T23:13:53-08:00","id":1498821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498817#post1498817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Makes sense, I'll bump that up to the 5th attainment then I think</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. You could drop Instant Casting to keep it at Adept","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T23:25:45-08:00","id":1498822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1498821#post1498821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair. You could drop Instant Casting to keep it at Adept</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do like that better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T16:17:54-08:00","id":1499102,"title":"","content":"I think this is finished!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T16:42:03-08:00","id":1499104,"title":"","content":"That seems... overpowered. I mean, granted, it's a Capstone, but instantly killing anything with less than five Stamina (since I assume this is Potency-primary) doesn't really line up with the Forces attack spells one would expect to see modeled.<br /> <br /> Also doesn't quite have anything to do with Forces. I guess you can swing <u>Create Energy</u> making a sudden burst of intense flame? Maybe? But that would still only account for disposing of a body, rather than insta-gibbing people. <u>Create Energy</u> doesn't even technically have enough Potency at Potency 5 to instantly incinerate a human body, and Matter's <u>Annihilate Matter</u> is the closest I can think of to achieve it.<br /> <br /> <u>Electromagnetic Pulse</u> might be more in-line with the rest of the Legacy, and it can double as an attack if needed. Then you just <u>Teleport</u> the body away","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":".  Annihilate Matter, not Ex Nihilo 12-08-2022, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T17:09:10-08:00","id":1499105,"title":"","content":"The capstone Attainment being <i>Eradicate Energy</i> doesn't make much thematic sense. They focus on deception, information gathering and infiltration. Assassination doesn't seem like the apex of their skill. I would instead recommend the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1416788#post1416788\">Hologram spell</a>. This allows them to create disposable disguises by layering it unto them, falsify documents as harmless magazines, transform their IDs into whatever they need. Used on another agent, a sound one can send one way messages. It has tons of useful applications and leaves no evidence, I think it would suit their modus operandi well. Reach could be assigned to instant use and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> So they are priorixing the quick escape of teleportation if things go FUBAR rather than the portal network? Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 12-07-2022, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T20:57:58-08:00","id":1499116,"title":"","content":"Nah I like it. I hear what you are saying, it does seem out of left field until you consider the surveillance state (their holy goal) being an authoritarian state, these states need executioners, they <i>need </i>secret police to make people disappear. The highest of their order carry out that roll without leaving a trace.<br /> <br /> And being you need gnosis...8 I believe in order to have that.<br /> <br /> I thought about Electromagnetic Pulse but decided against it. These guys <i>want </i>a world where these machines they use are running properly and have been invisible since the second attainment, while it feels cool it isn't really what they need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T21:16:09-08:00","id":1499117,"title":"","content":"It's <i>wierdly</i> out of left-field though. Like... the other Attainments are focused on seeing without being seen. Then the Capstone is... Kill? And &quot;Kill&quot; in a way that doesn't really jive with Forces, at that. Attainment-izing a direct damage spell would be the simpler option; two shots of <u>Thunderbolt</u> will end most human-adjascent Supernaturals for the low net cost of two Mana. Costless one-shot instant-kill, regardless of the target's actual health, really doesn't align with the normal scope of the setting.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you could get much better milage out of an insta-gib by <u>Teleport</u>ing someone to low-earth orbit. Or the Mariana Trench. Or the sun. Or even just a <u>Pocket Dimension</u> you've set up specifically for this purpose.<br /> <br /> It's your Legacy, so I'm obviously not demanding you change it. It's just... not a choice I understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-08-2022, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T22:19:44-08:00","id":1499123,"title":"","content":"No worries, I know you're offering advice not making demands. I'll sleep on your advice but I really do believe the attainment fits the theme of the legacy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T00:13:33-08:00","id":1499129,"title":"","content":"TL/DR: if you're keeping the &quot;kill&quot; ability, I recommend just Attainment-izing <u>Thunderbolt</u>, and disposing of the bodies with the <u>Teleport</u> Attainment.<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> I feel I should specify; it's not the killing part that worries me. I don't care much for &quot;buiser&quot; Legacies in general, because they tend to be boring, but I can see how the people this Legacy would attract would end up here. A little wierd to waste cosmic enlightenment of murderhoboing, but... Hubris. A Gnosis 8 Forces 5 Mage should really have more creative ways to deal with their enemies though.<br /> <br /> No, what worries me is the <i>instant kill</i>. <s>An Attainment shouldn't be drastically stronger than a spell, and I can't recall anything that just kills opponents outright. An Adept direct damage spell can <i>effectively</i> kill the average person in one hit (Potency 7, and Reach+Mana for Aggravated Damage) but still leaves wiggle room for outliers to survive without being a ST fiat. It also doesn't do so for free - even as an Attainment it would cost a point of Mana to do Aggravated. That makes for a more interesting character, in my opinion. Either the Attainment spent the Reach on Agg Damage and Instant Casting, in which case it needs to be Touch/Aimed, or it only does Lethal but can be cast at Sight Range instantly. The first means you have to get close and can't just spam it indiscriminately, while the second means you can't kill people as quickly, but you can be a <i>bastard</i> to try and even pin down while whittling them away.</s> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> pointed out to me that <u>Eradicate Energy</u> can instantly kill someone. Fair enough - my position will remain that murder is a boring Capstone.<br /> <br /> The disintegration effect is strange too. Human fat can combust around the 250C mark (someone sciency and/or psychopathic correct me on that plz) and requires a fairly consistent temperature to be fully consumed. <u>Create Energy</u> is the nearest Forces effect that could create something like that, but with Instant Casting you can't get a high enough Potency to pull it off. <u>Annihilate Matter</u> from Matter can erase bodies (and other objects), but Forces shouldn't be able to just disintegrate a body, especially as a secondary effect. And it IS a secondary effect: the primary is &quot;kill this thing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-08-2022, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T04:41:24-08:00","id":1499137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499117#post1499117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, you could get much better milage out of an insta-gib by <u>Teleport</u>ing someone to low-earth orbit. Or the Mariana Trench. Or the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not how Teleportation beyond Sensory range works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T12:47:54-08:00","id":1499159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499137#post1499137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not how Teleportation beyond Sensory range works.</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Web Weaver</u> with the Time conjunctive effect to give yourself Sympathy to places you've been to before seems fairly consistent with RAW. The sun might be a bit difficult, but not insurmountable.<br /> <br /> Or, hell, in this particular scenario we're talking about a Master of Space. They could just use <u>Create Sympathy</u> when visiting somewhere dangerous.<br /> <br /> Or, even simpler: give yourself Sympathy to a beacon. Get Sympathy to a satellite before it launches into space, and you've got a connection to low-eath orbit. Sympathy to a lead weight, and drop it into the Trench. Now whatever you teleport ends up in the immediate proximity of the beacon.<br /> <br /> <u>Teleportation</u> only requires you to have Sympathy to whichever of the subject or destination is beyond Sensory range, so laying hands on a target and teleporting them into the stretch of the Mariana Trench that you've given yourself Sympathy to is absolutely how it works, unless I've missed some glaring line of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-08-2022, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T12:58:56-08:00","id":1499161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499159#post1499159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>Web Weaver</u> with the Time conjunctive effect to give yourself Sympathy to places you've been to before seems fairly consistent with RAW. The sun might be a bit difficult, but not insurmountable.<br /> <br /> Or, hell, in this particular scenario we're talking about a Master of Space. They could just use <u>Create Sympathy</u> when visiting somewhere dangerous.<br /> <br /> Or, even simpler: give yourself Sympathy to a beacon. Get Sympathy to a satellite before it launches into space, and you've got a connection to low-eath orbit. Sympathy to a lead weight, and drop it into the Trench. Now whatever you teleport ends up in the immediate proximity of the beacon.<br /> <br /> <u>Teleportation</u> only requires you to have Sympathy to whichever of the subject or destination is beyond Sensory range, so laying hands on a target and teleporting them into the stretch of the Mariana Trench that you've given yourself Sympathy to is absolutely how it works, unless I've missed some glaring line of text.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A photo of the surface of the sun from a science book might work. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T13:42:14-08:00","id":1499167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499161#post1499161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A photo of the surface of the sun from a science book might work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need a sympathetic connection. The photo works as a sympathy yantra; nothing more. (Though, for the sun, a circle drawn with a yellow crayon would be a valid sympathy yantra.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T16:25:29-08:00","id":1499173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499159#post1499159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Web Weaver</u> with the Time conjunctive effect to give yourself Sympathy to places you've been to before seems fairly consistent with RAW. The sun might be a bit difficult, but not insurmountable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would need to have been to the Sun and use a sympathy Yantra representative of that time you went to the Sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, hell, in this particular scenario we're talking about a Master of Space. They could just use <u>Create Sympathy</u> when visiting somewhere dangerous.<br /> <br /> Or, even simpler: give yourself Sympathy to a beacon. Get Sympathy to a satellite before it launches into space, and you've got a connection to low-eath orbit. Sympathy to a lead weight, and drop it into the Trench. Now whatever you teleport ends up in the immediate proximity of the beacon.<br /> <br /> <u>Teleportation</u> only requires you to have Sympathy to whichever of the subject or destination is beyond Sensory range, so laying hands on a target and teleporting them into the stretch of the Mariana Trench that you've given yourself Sympathy to is absolutely how it works, unless I've missed some glaring line of text. </div> </div> </div>The glaring thing you've missed within the text is that this has now become a thing requiring at least one extra step that an Attainment probably shouldn't be assumed to need to engage, particularly since, as Tessie rightly observes, you'd still need a sympathy Yantra.<br /> <br /> Unless your proposal is that all of these Cold War-era surveillance aficionados have been to the Sun/the Mariana Trench/low Earth orbit for some reason, Eradicate Energy is the tidier form of instant-kill to use. The default assumption is not that your thirty-seven step secret plan is already prepared for your spells to exploit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T16:39:45-08:00","id":1499174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499173#post1499173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would need to have been to the Sun and use a sympathy Yantra representative of that time you went to the Sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Teleport to the sun&quot; does not have to literally be the surface of the sun. As with the satellite in near-earth orbit, you could do the same thing with a probe that's in the solar neighborhood for effectively the same result.<br /> <br /> And if we're really being pedantic, this is a Legacy that descends partially from the Panopticon. The Prelacy Crown of which is pretty darn terrifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499173#post1499173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The glaring thing you've missed within the text is that this has now become a thing requiring at least one extra step that an Attainment probably shouldn't be assumed to need to engage, particularly since, as Tessie rightly observes, you'd still need a sympathy Yantra.<br /> <br /> Unless your proposal is that all of these Cold War-era surveillance aficionados have been to the Sun/the Mariana Trench/low Earth orbit for some reason, Eradicate Energy is the tidier form of instant-kill to use. The default assumption is not that your thirty-seven step secret plan is already prepared for your spells to exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was the less dramatic &quot;teleport the body to a different location&quot;. I chose &quot;the sun&quot; or &quot;the Mariana Trench&quot; because the hyperbole is far more evocative. <br /> <br /> Besides which, the main thrust of my arguement was that &quot;My character / the DMPC kills this character and disposes of the body with a single touch&quot; is far less interesting than &quot;I killed this person with a touch and now need to dispose of the body&quot;. Yes, disposal in the second case still only takes a few turns, but it has more flavor and chance to get caught in the act than a disintegration ray that doesn't even line up with the proposed application of Forces.<br /> <br /> Know what? Fuck it. Dealing with Satchel is far more hassle than it's worth. Ignore list it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 12-09-2022, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T18:11:21-08:00","id":1499178,"title":"","content":"After thinking on it all day I like the ability to just fry someone, allowing the highest ranks to act as someone who &quot;disappears&quot; the enemies of the state they work for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T18:11:51-08:00","id":1499179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499174#post1499174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Teleport to the sun&quot; does not have to literally be the surface of the sun. As with the satellite in near-earth orbit, you could do the same thing with a probe that's in the solar neighborhood for effectively the same result.</div> </div> </div> </div>And a similar degree of legwork, neither of which comes implicit in the usual statement of &quot;teleport it to the Sun to kill it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if we're really being pedantic, this I'd a Legacy that descends partially from the Panopticon. The Prelacy Crown of which is pretty darn terrifying. </div> </div> </div>We can get even more pedantic and point out that a location is not a subject, but also this sounds more like an argument <i>against</i> a Teleportation-based killing Attainment where the non-Seer half of the Legacy still exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point was the less dramatic &quot;teleport the body to a different location&quot;. I chose &quot;the sun&quot; or &quot;the Mariana Trench&quot; because the hyperbole is far more evocative. </div> </div> </div>I would recommend avoiding it in the future because of this specific derailment. Enough people overestimate the baseline capabilities of the Awakened template without immediately Going To Space with your examples. &quot;Your Sanctum's incinerator/drowning tank/death trap&quot; gets the point across.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides which, the main thrust of my arguement was that &quot;My character / the DMPC kills this character and disposes of the body with a single touch&quot; is far less interesting than &quot;I killed this person with a touch and now need to dispose of the body&quot;. Yes, disposal in the second case still only takes a few turns, but it has more flavor and chance to get caught in the act than a disintegration ray that doesn't even line up with the proposed application of Forces. </div> </div> </div>Blades in the Dark, a game where bodies need to be specially cremated to prevent ghosts from rising and magical animals can track the location of the recently deceased, provides its Assassin crew type with advancement options to circumvent both of these through &quot;hard-won experience or occult ritual,&quot; and there are systems in that game specifically built around minimizing the attention you draw (when killing happening at all during a heist you were on draws attention whether you're the ones who did it or not). Much as I would love for Chronicles to have a generalized attention/exposure system to hook stuff like the Masquerade and the Veil and Cover and whatnot into, it is not a system whereby the default assumption is that extremely powerful monsters still need to go out of their way to hide a body, especially when those monsters truck with the lore that bends light and stokes flames and holds things together.<br /> <br /> The thrust of your argument is &quot;A Gnosis 8 Master of an Arcanum at the apex of their Legacy's Attainments can disintegrate someone with a touch and that's less interesting than needing to worry about body disposal in a game where magic can do a great deal and I've just spent multiple posts talking about how with a bunch of previously-unstated prep you could get better mileage by teleporting them somewhere unpleasant that you have the sympathies for.&quot;<br /> <br /> I agree that From Dust to Ash is a bit out of left-field after the preceding Attainments. I strongly disagree that fatal use of Teleportation is a superior use of Legacy-building resources to the same end.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26284_6.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26284\" data-vbnamecard=\"26284\">Aendrinastor</a> Sorry to repeat this question, since it seems to have been lost behind my other one, but: what's the Theory of magic that the Glasaugen perspective is built on, beyond the basic Panopticon premise?<br /> <br /> Also if that is the Theory, would it not make sense for at least some of their Attainments to involve or at least facilitate having subjects know or feel they're being watched?<br /> <br /> Less pressingly, how are they organized?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T18:14:50-08:00","id":1499181,"title":"","content":"Appreciate all the advice you've given guys <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T19:14:29-08:00","id":1499183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499179#post1499179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26284_6.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26284\" data-vbnamecard=\"26284\">Aendrinastor</a> Sorry to repeat this question, since it seems to have been lost behind my other one, but: what's the Theory of magic that the Glasaugen perspective is built on, beyond the basic Panopticon premise?<br /> <br /> Also if that is the Theory, would it not make sense for at least some of their Attainments to involve or at least facilitate having subjects know or feel they're being watched?<br /> <br /> Less pressingly, how are they organized?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Organization is very top down. The higher ups have all the information, they give it out to the ones further down on the totem pole as needed for missions and nothing more. Think CIA director vs field agent dynamic.<br /> <br /> As for their theory of magic...they kind of won it. They want a camera on every street corner, reminding everyone that they are always being watched. These guys have won the philosophical war, now its about maintaining it and using it.<br /> <br /> If you were to play a Dark Eras game set during the Cold War when these guys were developing their philosophy would be about building the infrastructure and reputation of the governments they found themselves in to cause the idea that they are always being watched. IDK how the Panaopticon functioned before a surveillance state existed but these guys, I'd say, are responsible for how they function now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T19:49:52-08:00","id":1499186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499183#post1499183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for their theory of magic...they kind of won it. They want a camera on every street corner, reminding everyone that they are always being watched. These guys have won the philosophical war, now its about maintaining it and using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to say that this doesn't exactly answer the question.<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question believe that all evidence contributes holistic clues to an ultimate truth; the Legacy that was consumed to create the Tremere House Thrax believes that having the power of life and death over somebody gives you mystical access to their strength; the Keepers of Vedet (later House Vedmak) explained their magic in terms of cultivating spiritual sensitivity in order to steal the powers of ghosts and spirits.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking about their goals, I'm asking what the magical beliefs of the Glass Eyes are that are expressed through their Attainments, as distinct from the basic premise of the Panopticon Ministry's favored axis of control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T05:42:29-08:00","id":1499212,"title":"","content":"Looking at the intro and the Attainments, I\u2019d say their magical theory is about dissection and digestion of data. You dig dirt until you hit the gold.<br /> <br /> This would also explain why their Fifth Attainment is a killing touch; you don\u2019t need all the dug-out dirt. Nor the shaft, for that matter. (Still would be nice trying to explain this from a Forces perspective, though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T14:55:12-08:00","id":1499250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499186#post1499186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not asking about their goals, I'm asking what the magical beliefs of the Glass Eyes are that are expressed through their Attainments, as distinct from the basic premise of the Panopticon Ministry's favored axis of control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic is holy when only the one doing the magic can see it<br /> When the person who is being affected by magic has no clue the magic is happened, that <i>is</i> divinity. It is not divine in the sense that it is next to god, inspired by god, or a reflection of divinity. It is divinity within the fallen world<br /> <br /> I'll be honest I hadn't really thought of that, so this is a first draft of the idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T21:39:37-08:00","id":1499268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499186#post1499186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to say that this doesn't exactly answer the question.<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question believe that all evidence contributes holistic clues to an ultimate truth; the Legacy that was consumed to create the Tremere House Thrax believes that having the power of life and death over somebody gives you mystical access to their strength; the Keepers of Vedet (later House Vedmak) explained their magic in terms of cultivating spiritual sensitivity in order to steal the powers of ghosts and spirits.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking about their goals, I'm asking what the magical beliefs of the Glass Eyes are that are expressed through their Attainments, as distinct from the basic premise of the Panopticon Ministry's favored axis of control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I started working on three other legacy conversions today (A lot I know, but they are conversions, and for PCs I'm currently playing or will be playing) but thinking about the Glass Eyes view of magic as I go to give a better, more fleshed out answer<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T19:32:17-08:00","id":1504707,"title":"","content":"I don't think this will get me in trouble because this is still on the front page of the Mage forums, even if it is a few months old<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499186#post1499186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to say that this doesn't exactly answer the question.<br /> <br /> The Eleventh Question believe that all evidence contributes holistic clues to an ultimate truth; the Legacy that was consumed to create the Tremere House Thrax believes that having the power of life and death over somebody gives you mystical access to their strength; the Keepers of Vedet (later House Vedmak) explained their magic in terms of cultivating spiritual sensitivity in order to steal the powers of ghosts and spirits.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking about their goals, I'm asking what the magical beliefs of the Glass Eyes are that are expressed through their Attainments, as distinct from the basic premise of the Panopticon Ministry's favored axis of control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is a long over due response but I moved on to other things over Christmas while the forums were down and then forgot to come back and give an update, so here I am as I'm working on finishing this up.<br /> <br /> Magic, to The Glasaugen, is an expression of knowledge. Not abstract or philosophical knowledge, but useful, practical knowledge about a someone or something. You study a person, place, or thing (from the shadows) in order to build up a parasocial sympathetic connection to them so that you can preform magic, but the construction of that sort of sympathy is also magic. Parasocial sympathy is something I will be going back in the original writeup to add in to their philosophy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Magic is holy when only the one doing the magic can see it<br /> When the person who is being affected by magic has no clue the magic is happened, that <i>is</i> divinity. It is not divine in the sense that it is next to god, inspired by god, or a reflection of divinity. It is divinity within the fallen world&quot; - This is still true for them<br /> <br /> Magic is parasocial and unseen by all but the one casting, that is where you will find Truth.<br /> <br /> <i>Still</i> a work in progress but now that I'm back to working on this I believe I'll get it more fleshed out. \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1498727-the-glasaugen-mastigos-forces-space-homebrew-legacy?p=1499105#post1499105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they are priorixing the quick escape of teleportation if things go FUBAR rather than the portal network? Makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started working on this again this weekend and decided I <u><i>really</i></u> like the portal network idea you gave, so I actually changed it to reflect that ability\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}